WEBVTT

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.690
I have a name for you.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.600
From now on, you are Yuzu.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:11.000
<b>Konohana Kitan</b>

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:16.000
<b>Episode 6: 
Konohanatei Horror Stories</b>

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.620
There was once a girl who 
didn't have any family.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.370
She had no friends either, 
and she spent all her time alone.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:32.830
She did what she could to make friends, 
but no one truly loved her.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.330
Why am I not good enough?

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.500
What do I have to change about myself?

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.520
Is it because I'm me?

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.150
Should I become someone else?

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.820
With that idea,

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.410
believing she could become 
someone else if she erased herself...

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:55.410
Hey, am I the person you want now?

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.880
Will you like me now?

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.870
Why are you running away?

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.470
Am I still not good enough?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.140
Tell me you like me.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.390
Then you can become like me.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.320
Why are you still up?!

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.320
S...

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:13.910
S...

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:14.460
S...

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.090
S...

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:15.780
S...

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.720
Sorry.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.210
Sheesh.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.190
They just think staying up late 
won't ruin their complexion.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.010
Damn, Okami!

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.400
She's five times more powerful at night!

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.320
Shall we call it a night?

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.840
That was fun.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.080
Satsuki and Okiku should have come...

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:36.800
Huh?

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:37.870
What is it?

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.750
One, two, three, four, five...

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.180
There's one extra.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:45.990
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:46.430
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.890
Holy crap!

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.340
This isn't funny!

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.320
What is going on?

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:01.020
The lights are out all over the building!

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:01.780
Yeah.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.770
We were telling horror stories, 
and an actual ghost showed up.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.860
Please stop talking about that.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.530
All right, ghosts aside,

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.750
everyone split up to turn the lights back 
on and make sure the guests are safe.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:14.610
Got it?

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:15.450
Okay.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.320
Satsuki, you... never mind.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:18.410
I can!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.370
I can do it.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:24.090
I'll check the first floor with Yuzu.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.130
Okay.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.770
If you see a ghost, get rid of it.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.950
Come on, I'd rather catch it.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.550
Oh, dear.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.420
It's so quiet.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:45.940
One time when I was little, I napped 
too long and couldn't sleep at night.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:52.800
I got lonely being by myself at night, 
so I asked Bikuni-sama to stay with me.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:58.430
When that clock strikes twelve, 
today ends, and tomorrow comes.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:02.950
You know how it's morning when 
you wake up and it's "tomorrow"?

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:06.080
No, I think the new morning is "today."

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.640
That's right.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.570
It's always "today" before you even notice.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.000
So?

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.320
Where does tomorrow come from?

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:18.310
Who's switching today out with tomorrow?

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:21.300
It was a very, very strange trick.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.860
I felt like I'd gotten to see 
one of the world's secrets.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:31.600
On a special night like tonight, I feel 
like another secret is hiding somewhere.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.030
It makes me so excited.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:37.240
Oh, yeah. You said you 
were raised by a human.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:38.000
Yes.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.700
I was adopted.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.160
Adopted?

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:50.760
Satsuki-chan?

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.740
A weird sound is coming out of you.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.450
I'm fine.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:00.860
Um, Satsuki-chan, are you afraid of gho—

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:01.680
No!

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:05.950
Of course.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.650
Stop being silly. Let's go.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.610
Did someone just...

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.040
Satsuki-chan...

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.750
I-I'm not afraid of ghosts! I'm not!

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:26.290
<i>She's shaking.</i>

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.060
<i>She's so thin.</i>

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:29.200
<i>So soft...</i>

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:34.400
<i>Satsuki-chan's an amazing person, 
but she's still just a normal girl.</i>

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:37.130
Yes, I know.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.090
It's okay.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.050
Why are you two getting all cuddly here?

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.900
We're not cuddling!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.890
Give me that!

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.960
You, too. Get up and...

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.400
Why are you laughing?

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:54.860
It's nothing.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.910
<i>See, on special nights like this one,</i>

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.320
<i>you can find secrets that 
you don't see in the sunlight.</i>

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.310
Hey, have you seen Ren?

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:04.720
We got split up.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.040
No, I haven't seen her.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.970
She's such a scaredy-cat.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:10.770
She even told me not to let go of her hand...

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:15.530
Hey, Nacchan, you'd better 
not let go of my hand.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:16.410
Sure.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:18.450
And walk a little slower.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:19.790
You're going too fast.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:20.610
Sure.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.870
You don't have to stop.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.380
Nacchan?

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:35.400
Ren, do you like me?

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:39.110
Wh-Wh-What are you saying 
in a place like this?!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.080
Do you?

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:46.060
<i>She's so awesome. She's so 
awesome. She's so awesome.</i>

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.500
<i>We can't be doing this while we're working.</i>

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.720
<i>But I kind of like that sense of shame...</i>

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.170
<i>What's wrong with her?</i>

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:58.880
<i>Did she get food poisoning from 
the miso mackerel we had for dinner?</i>

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:02.340
<i>I should have brushed my teeth!</i>

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:04.350
<i>She's so close!</i>

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.070
<i>Her face...</i>

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.480
<i>Oh my God, she's so awesome!</i>

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.830
<i>Damn it, just go for it!</i>

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:10.760
<i>I love you.</i>

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:21.250
I-I'm sorry we were making so much noise.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.210
No, thank you for that.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:28.920
Thank...

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.020
H-How could she make fun of me like that?

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:40.770
It's not like I'm disappointed 
by it or anything!

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:42.140
Not really...

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:50.470
It's such a pain, going around 
and turning on all the lights.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.470
No!

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:31.020
Stay away!

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:35.680
It's a lot brighter now.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.680
I'm not scared or anything.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.990
I'm just a bit sc— I just don't like it.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:41.910
Kiri?

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.890
You're the ghost Natsume was talking about.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.510
How did you find out?

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.560
I didn't have to.

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.890
You just lost your edge.

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:16.160
You got gross, so I whacked you.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.360
What's up?

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.960
Natsume, help me out.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.150
Let's catch it.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:22.030
Sure!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.730
I thought you were afraid of me.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.550
Well, too bad.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:30.500
I'm not af— It's not ghosts that I hate.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.880
It's the darkness.

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:37.710
Why would you tell the enemy your weakness?!

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.080
You're the worst!

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:46.170
How could you do that after 
what you did to me? You pervert!

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:48.050
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:49.480
Shut up, idiot!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.990
Go ask your own d#&@!

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.720
But I don't have one.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:56.220
Hey, now.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:57.940
It's late.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.180
Quiet down.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.390
Huh?

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:01.780
What...

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.570
Two Kiri-neesamas?

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.270
Which one's real?

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.780
We could check by stripping her down.

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:19.410
There's something hot about 
playing with your own body.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:20.550
That settles it.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.960
You're the real one.

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.880
It's running away! After it!

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:31.100
It's just a ghost. Leave it.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.560
It's ghost season. What can you do?

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:34.850
They're seasonal?!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:39.000
This is all because you guys 
were telling horror stories.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:41.170
Stop!

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:44.990
Huh?

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:45.880
Where's Yuzu?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.880
Oh, yeah. Where did she go?

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.000
Hey... Where are we going?

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.630
Somewhere happy.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.960
You'd come with me, right?

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.910
Yes, I'll come with you.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:07.340
By the way, who are you?

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.050
You noticed?

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:16.340
You came with me knowing I'm an impostor?

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:22.100
I couldn't say no to a face like that.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.460
You were adopted?

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:28.460
Yes, I was stuck in the snow by myself, 
and that's when Bikuni-sama took me in.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:29.960
By yourself?

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:31.320
I see.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.780
Would you come to like me?

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.370
Who would I have to be for you to like me?

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.220
What should I change about myself?

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.960
Just tell me that, and...

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:47.160
Who do you like?

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.010
I...

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:50.630
Then what about you?

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:53.190
Me? I...

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.550
I hate that man.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.600
Yohei-san, you mean?

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.270
He makes fun of me.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.730
Hey, it's Bikuni-sama's errand fox.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.890
You're slow as always.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.860
Don't sulk.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.610
You'll get even uglier.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:18.870
He'd never have talked to me 
like that if I served an Inari shrine.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:22.540
Yuzu, can you read people's minds?

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.330
No.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:28.790
Then why do you say that 
as though it were truth?

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:33.690
I want you to learn to hear not just words, 
but the true thoughts behind them.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.340
I'm sorry.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:49.660
You'd better stop being useless, 
or you'll get kicked out of the temple.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:52.610
<i>That's crazy.</i>

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:55.470
<i>Bikuni-sama would never kick me out.</i>

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:59.700
The Inari shrine in my town 
is short on manpower.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.790
Or should I say foxpower?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.780
Why don't you have Yuzu work there?

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:06.960
Indeed.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.260
I'll think about it.

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:22.220
Yeah, that's the thing. I was just...

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.200
Yo, Yuzu-bou.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.820
Working hard as always, huh?

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.140
What's wrong with her?

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.480
She looked upset.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.700
What was that noise, Yuzu?

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.420
Yuzu!

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.870
I-I was trying to wipe the Buddha.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.750
Bikuni-sama!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:49.930
Oh, dear.

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:51.100
Are you hurt?

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:53.130
I'm sorry.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:55.330
I'll be more careful.

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.550
I'll work even harder.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:01.530
So please let me stay with you!

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.990
What makes you say that?

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.420
Because I'm useless.

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:10.920
That's why you're going to send me away...

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.300
Look, Yuzu.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:25.290
Do you think that flower is useless?

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:31.800
No, the flowers are pretty, and they 
smell nice, and they heal the mind.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:36.550
But they aren't there only for 
the sake of our enjoyment.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.450
The nectar and scent both attract insects.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.180
It's so that they can propagate.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.460
The flowers themselves 
surely don't know that they

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.810
eased someone's mind 
and gave them strength.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:51.370
That's too complicated. I don't get it.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:58.820
Didn't you say no one would make fun 
of you if you served an Inari shrine?

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:05.940
I thought, if that would give you confidence,
it might be worth sending you off.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.230
But as you are now, I worry.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:13.710
Continue to serve me from now on, Yuzu.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.010
Bikuni-sama!

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.190
Past that mountain and further still,

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:32.110
at the top of a large post town, 
there's a splendid inn.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.180
Are you talking about Konohanatei?

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:37.310
You know of it, too?

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:40.920
I've been long acquainted 
with the okami there.

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:45.060
I've only been there once, 
but man, it was exceptional.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.260
Thank you.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.190
You're that little fox from way back.

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.250
You've grown quite a bit.

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:54.580
Yes.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:59.170
Oh, right. There are a lot of 
adorable fox attendants there.

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:01.960
They're all about your age.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:04.680
Foxes? About my age?

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:06.960
I said to the head attendant,

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:10.910
"It must be tough, dealing with 
different guests every day."

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.850
That's what makes it enjoyable.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:21.580
If, when you're tired, when you're in pain, 
you can recall your dreamlike visit here,

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:27.500
Konohanatei will stay as brilliant in your 
heart as flower blossoms in full bloom.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.980
Nothing would bring me, as an attendant,

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.670
more joy than if you can 
make such a memory here.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.170
...she said.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.750
<i>Past that mountain and further still...</i>

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:48.870
Yuzu.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:50.190
Yuzu.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:53.530
I-I'm sorry.

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:55.540
I was studying properly.

00:18:55.540 --> 00:19:00.230
To learn is not only to gain 
knowledge atop a desk.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:04.190
You must go and learn from 
many other souls, Yuzu.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.290
That's something you 
could do at Konohanatei.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.620
Konohanatei...

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:15.190
Do you mean it, Bikuni-sama?

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:18.550
Remember what I said about the flowers?

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:22.260
You are those flowers to me, Yuzu.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:25.720
That's why I'm sending you off.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:34.160
So that you can bloom even more proudly.

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.220
Bikuni-sama!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:42.270
Huh?

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:46.660
Was I just dreaming standing up?

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:49.870
You haven't given me an answer.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.900
Who do you like?

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:54.090
A lot of people.

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:58.700
Bikuni-sama, the people who visit the temple,

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:02.410
the people at Konohanatei, the guests here...

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:08.460
A slight change in circumstances, 
and I might have never met any of them.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:15.090
Just being with them fills me 
with gratitude for that miracle.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.000
And today, I met you.

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.620
I wanted to meet you, too.

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:25.100
But earlier.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:26.150
A boat?

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:27.630
Are you getting on?

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:30.860
I'm headed to the happy place you wanted.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.090
Yeah.

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:45.840
Hey, Yuzu, what would you do if I didn't let 
go of your hand until we got to the other side?

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:49.800
I'd come with you to the other 
side, and then come back.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:52.680
I'm sorry for peeping on you.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:53.760
Peeping?

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:58.490
I hope I can put on beautiful 
flowers next time.

00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:02.900
Let's meet again, Yuzu.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:10.480
With a smile like that, I'm sure 
you can make everyone love you.

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:15.360
You don't need to be anyone else.

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:18.400
Oh? I see.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:21.430
And that's why you came home in the morning?

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:22.210
Yes.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.940
You've sure got guts, though, Yun-tan.

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:26.660
You're not scared of ghosts?

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.130
Ghosts?

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.750
Oh, you mean how she took on other forms?

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:34.790
That's right. She was good at imitating people.

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:36.100
Um...

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.240
The girl you sent off...

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:41.020
She was a ghost. An evil spirit. Get it?

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:44.640
That was a close one, though.

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:47.320
She crossed a river, didn't she?

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.070
Yes.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:50.730
That was the River Styx.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:59.650
<i>That was the story of a slightly odd night 
of my first summer at Konohanatei.</i>

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:01.540
The end.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.010
<b>Konohanatei 
Horror 
Stories</b>

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.010
<b>The End</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Episode: 
Night of the Summer Festival</b>
